    <div class="tool-shell tool-prompt-shell">
      <div class="tool-main-row">
        <label for="__DOM_PREFIX__Prompt" class="tool-main-label">Architecture prompt</label>
        <div class="tool-main-input-grid __PREFIX__-main-input-grid">
          <textarea
            id="__DOM_PREFIX__Prompt"
            class="form-control __PREFIX__-prompt"
            placeholder="Describe the AWS VPC layout, region, availability zones, ingress path, compute tier, database tier, and shared services."
          >Create an AWS VPC architecture in us-east-1 with 2 availability zones. Use public subnets for an internet-facing Application Load Balancer, private app subnets for EC2 application servers, and private data subnets for a Multi-AZ RDS PostgreSQL database. Add a single NAT gateway, VPC endpoints for S3 and Systems Manager, CloudWatch, and VPC flow logs.</textarea>

        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="tool-control-hint __PREFIX__-prompt-hint">
        Use one brief prompt with region, AZ count, ingress, private tiers, and supporting AWS services. Presets below can prefill and instantly generate a working layout.
      </p>

      <div class="__PREFIX__-main-actions">
        <button type="button" class="tool-action-btn tool-action-btn-primary" id="__DOM_PREFIX__Generate">
          <i class="bi bi-stars" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <span>Generate Diagram</span>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="tool-action-btn tool-action-btn-secondary" id="__DOM_PREFIX__Reset">Load Default</button>
      </div>
    </div>
